 "split": "setup_long",
 "sentences": [
  "First, it's crucial to set clear goals and expectations.",
  "We'll ensure that our tasks and deadlines are well-defined, and we'll regularly touch base to discuss progress and address any concerns.",
  "When working remotely, we can't pop by each other's desks to clarify something quickly.",
  "So, we need to ensure that we provide detailed context and explanations in our messages and emails.",
  "This reduces confusion and prevents misunderstandings.",
  "Well, one crucial practice is maintaining regular work hours, even when working remotely.",
  "It's easy to fall into the trap of working extended hours or feeling like you need to be constantly available.",
  "Setting boundaries and sticking to your work schedule is important for maintaining a healthy work-life balance.",
  "In Python, we always include docstrings in our methods to provide clear and concise documentation.",
  "It's important to stay secure, especially in our line of work.",
  "I want you to focus on the former and avoid the latter.",
  "Imagine you're making a quick change to a single file, but then you have to wait for a pre-commit hook to run a full suite of tests or linters.",
  "Now, post-commit hooks are more flexible.",
  "They let you perform actions after you've committed your changes, without interrupting your workflow.",
  "It's all about efficiency and maintaining a smooth workflow.",
  "So, going forward, I want you to focus on utilizing post-commit hooks.",
  "If there are specific checks or tasks you want to perform before committing, integrate them into your daily routine or your text editor's settings."
 ],
